Package: MGmixIRT
Type: Package
Title: Multigroup Mixture Item Response Theory Models for Performance Decline
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Mehmet Cahit", "Marangoz", email = "cahitgs@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimation of multigroup mixture item response theory models for
    performance decline and aberrant response behaviour in low-stakes
    assessments. Implements multigroup extensions of the two-class mixture
    model of Bolt, Cohen, and Wollack (2002) <doi:10.1111/j.1745-3984.2002.tb01146.x>,
    the HYBRID model of Yamamoto (1995), and the multiclass performance
    decline model of Jin and Wang (2014) <doi:10.1111/jedm.12041>, following
    the general framework of List, Robitzsch, Luedtke, Koeller, and Nagy
    (2017) <doi:10.1186/s40536-017-0049-3>. Models are estimated by marginal
    maximum likelihood with an EM algorithm and Gauss-Hermite quadrature.
    Class probabilities can follow the parsimonious shape-parameter
    formulation of Cao and Stokes (2008) <doi:10.1007/s11336-007-9045-9>.
